{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 15, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B15", "text_preview": "Schema.org for Developers"}
{"kind": "heading", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 16, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B16", "text_preview": "Extensions"}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 17, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B17", "text_preview": "As schema.org has grown, we have explored various mechanisms for community extension as\n   a way of adding more detailed descriptive vocabulary that builds on the schema.org core. Some areas of Schema.org were\n   developed as \"named extensi"}
{"kind": "heading", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 18, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B18", "text_preview": "Hosted Sections"}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 19, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B19", "text_preview": "For example, via the auto section there is a property for emissionsCO2 ,\nand via the bib section we have a property publisherImprint .\nHowever, from the perspective of a publisher, these are simply schema.org properties."}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 20, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B20", "text_preview": "We have a few of these sections:"}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 21, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B21", "text_preview": "auto"}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 22, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B22", "text_preview": "bib"}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 23, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B23", "text_preview": "health-lifesci"}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 24, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B24", "text_preview": "meta"}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 25, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B25", "text_preview": "pending"}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 26, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B26", "text_preview": "Note : the 'pending' and 'meta' hosted sections are part of schema.org's schema development process."}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 27, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B27", "text_preview": "We use the ' pending ' section as a staging area for new schema.org terms that are under discussion and review.\n  Implementors and publishers are cautioned that terms in the pending section\n  may lack consensus and that terminology and defi"}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 28, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B28", "text_preview": "The ' meta ' section is primarily for vocabulary used internally within schema.org to support technical definitions and\nschema.org site functionality. These terms are not intended for general usage in the public Web."}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 29, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B29", "text_preview": "Attic is a special area where terms are archived when deprecated from the core and other sections, or removed from pending as not accepted into the full vocabulary. References to terms in the attic area are not normally displayed unless acc"}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 30, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B30", "text_preview": "Unlike other core and section terms, these areas may be updated at any time without the need for a full release ."}
{"kind": "heading", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 31, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B31", "text_preview": "External Extensions"}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 32, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B32", "text_preview": "The schema.org steering group does not officially approve external extensions - they are fully independent.\n  We list here some notable extensions that extend schema.org in interesting and useful ways."}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 33, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B33", "text_preview": "GS1 Web Vocabulary ( blog post )"}
{"kind": "paragraph", "local_path": "materialized_sources/corpus/vocabulary-schema.org--c8b3dc95/document.md", "ordinal": 34, "selector": "web://041bc69d51eac6de#B34", "text_preview": "Croissant is an open community-built standardized metadata vocabulary for ML datasets."}
